page 50"}, {"id": "f0500100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "IMPORTANCE OF JAMAAT", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": false, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "As has already been said in the foreword, there are many who say their salaat regularly but are not very particular about Jamaat. The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is as emphatic in enjoining Jamaat as he is particular about salaat. This part also consists of two chapters. The first deals with the rewards of Jamaat and the second with the consequences of its neglect.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "CHAPTER I", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": false, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "REWARDS OF JAMAAT", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": false, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith I", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": false, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عن ابن عمر رضي الله عنه أن رسول الله ﷺ قال صلاة الجماعة أفضل من صلاة الفذ بسبع وعشرين درجة رواه مالك والبخاري ومسلم والترمذي كذا في الترغيب", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}, {"id": "f0500700-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "b0500400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "translation", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abdullah bin Umar (Radhiyallaho anha) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying: \"A salaat with Jamaat is twenty-seven times superior to salaat performed individually.\"\n\nWhen we offer our salaat for getting reward from Allah, then why should it not be done in the musjid, where the reward earned is twenty-seven times more. Nobody will be so unwise as to forego a profit twenty-seven times greater with simply a little extra labour. But we are so indifferent about the profits promised for our religious practices! This can be due to nothing but our disregard for deen and the rewards of it. It is a pity that we apply ourselves so hard to acquiring the trifling gains in this material world; but are so unmindful of the gains in the Hereafter, which yield twenty-seven times more with a little extra effort. We often argue that for going to the musjid for Jamaat we have to close the shop and will thus lose business. These pretexts and others of the kind cannot stand in the way of those who have perfect faith in the Greatness of Allah, and", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 50"}]}'::jsonb);